---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for bellieacreswine.com — how Bellie Acres Wine collects, uses, and protects information, including Google AdSense."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 prose prose-stone">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif tracking-tight mb-2 not-prose">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 not-prose mb-10">Last updated: July 22, 2026 · Website: https://bellieacreswine.com</p>

    <p>
      Bellie Acres Wine (“we,” “us”) operates the independent Temecula Valley wine-country directory at
      <strong>bellieacreswine.com</strong>. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it,
      and the choices you have. By using the site, you agree to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      We publish travel and directory information about Temecula wineries, events, maps, and related experiences
      (such as hot-air balloon operators). We are not a winery, tasting room, or booking agency unless a page
      clearly says otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contact: <a href="mailto:lauradfarley@gmail.com">lauradfarley@gmail.com</a> ·
      <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Information you send us</strong> — name, email, and message content if you use our contact form or email us.</li>
      <li><strong>Automatic technical data</strong> — browser type, device, approximate location derived from IP, pages viewed, and referring URLs, typically via hosting logs (e.g. Netlify) and analytics/advertising partners.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies</strong> — used for site operation, preferences, analytics, and advertising (including Google AdSense).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website</li>
      <li>To respond to inquiries</li>
      <li>To understand aggregate traffic and content performance</li>
      <li>To display advertising (including personalized ads where permitted)</li>
      <li>To comply with law and enforce our Terms</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to show ads. Google and its partners may use cookies or device
      identifiers to serve ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can learn more and control ad
      personalization at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google’s Advertising policies</a>
      and
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to your website
      or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to your users
      based on their visit to your sites and/or other sites on the Internet. Users may opt out of personalized
      advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Our site is hosted on infrastructure that may log requests for security and reliability. We may use privacy-conscious
      or standard analytics tools in the future; if we add a named analytics product, we will update this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site discusses wine tourism and is intended for a general audience of adults. Alcohol tasting content is
      directed to people 21 years of age or older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you believe a child provided personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Contact emails are retained as long as needed to respond and keep basic business records. Server logs are retained
      according to our host’s defaults unless longer retention is required for security or legal reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Browser controls can block or delete cookies (some features or ads may not work as intended).</li>
      <li>Use Google Ads Settings / aboutads.info opt-outs for personalized ads where available.</li>
      <li>Email us to request access or deletion of personal information you sent us, subject to legal exceptions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      We link to winery websites, operators, and other external sites. Their privacy practices are their own. Review
      their policies before submitting information.
    </p>

    <h2>International visitors</h2>
    <p>
      The site is operated from the United States. If you access it from another country, you understand information
      may be processed in the U.S.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do.
      Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:lauradfarley@gmail.com">lauradfarley@gmail.com</a> or
      <a href="/contact">bellieacreswine.com/contact</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
